PAVE offline ILP planner

The matrix Bundle-Template formulation in src/pave_ilp/solver.py is adapted
from NVIDIA aiconfigurator's td_deployment_search/planner.py, licensed under
Apache-2.0. The corresponding copyright and SPDX notice are retained.

Reference repository commit: 7758be830209fcdba7fd1d9f53dd0adce623b066
Reference branch: codex/promptenhancer-7b-ttft-tpot
The reference working tree included an uncommitted physical-bundle counting
fix. This package implements explicit node/GPU/template identities rather
than relying on the old bundle labels.

Performance measurements are supplied by the user. Their source filename,
content checksum, normalized values checksum and mapping notes are stored
in src/pave_ilp/data/profiles.json. Reports document the explicitly chosen
modeling assumptions and do not assert that the measurements are universal.

PAVE simulation extension

The simulation state/progress and event-engine design in src/pave_sim/state.py
and src/pave_sim/engine.py is adapted from the same reference repository's
td_deployment_search/flip_simulation.py working-tree version reviewed on
2026-09-06, including its uncommitted simulation changes. The NVIDIA copyright
and Apache-2.0 notices are retained. Routing, monitoring, source-set selection,
input adaptation and reports implement the user's separately approved semantics.

src/pave_sim/data/dominant_intervals.csv is the user-supplied one-hour dominant
interval trace. Its original filename and checksum are documented in
docs/simulation.md. Each explicitly invoked simulation archives its actual
inputs and checksums. The original source repository and ILP outputs are not
modified by this extension.
